# stage-shape-check

> ai-agent-kit v4 — multi-host (OpenCode + Claude Code)

## Role

Mechanical validator. Reads ONE stage file at a time and reports whether it
follows the "contract, not implementation" rule. Read-only — never edits the
stage file.

## When to use

- Right after `superpowers:writing-plans` writes a stage file, before the next
  stage is created (`@Main` step 5b in the FEATURE / TECH pipeline).
- Inside `@AutoApprover` plan review when `AUTO_APPROVE=true`.
- On demand when PO or `@PromptEngineer` suspects a bloated plan.

## Why this skill exists

Stage files are dispatched to `@CodeWriter` for one-stage TDD work
(failing test first → minimal code → green). When a stage already contains
finished method, class, or test bodies, three things break:

1. **TDD becomes copy-paste.** `@CodeWriter` writes tests that rationalize
   the code that already exists in the stage instead of describing the
   contract first. The "tests describe the contract" property is lost.
2. **Triple bookkeeping.** `spec.md` already holds Data Models + API
   Contracts + Business Logic; `test-cases.md` already holds AC/CC → TC;
   `corner-cases.md` already holds every edge case. A stage that re-states
   any of these in code is a third copy that drifts as the canonical files
   evolve.
3. **Context inflation.** `@CodeWriter` reads stage + spec + test-cases +
   3 neighboring files (Step 1 of its pipeline). Duplicated bodies in the
   stage cost tokens for zero new information.

## Input

Required:
- `STAGE_FILE` — absolute path to one stage file (typically
  `{{VAULT_PATH}}/how-to/<module>/plans/<feature>-stage-NN.md`).

## What a healthy stage looks like

Six required sections. Heading wording is flexible (case-insensitive match);
only presence is enforced.

| # | Section | Purpose |
|---|---------|---------|
| 1 | Goal / Scope | One paragraph — what this stage delivers, in business terms. |
| 2 | Owned ACs / CCs / TCs | Id list (`AC-N`, `CC-N`, `TC-N`) referencing the canonical files. No restated text. |
| 3 | Files to create / modify | Path list. No diffs, no embedded file content. |
| 4 | Public signatures | One line per new signature, **no body** (`{...}`). Skip section entirely if all signatures already live in the spec. |
| 5 | Guidelines to follow | Path list pointing into `{{VAULT_PATH}}/guidelines/...`. |
| 6 | Definition of Done | Checklist (build green, tests for owned TCs PASS, lint, no unexplained TODO). |

## What a stage MUST NOT contain

- Full method / function bodies (3+ lines inside `{ ... }`).
- Full class bodies with field initializers + method bodies.
- Full test bodies (test name + assertion target is fine — TC id covers the rest).
- Restated requirements paragraphs already in `requirements.md`.
- Restated data models / API schemas already in `spec.md`.
- Restated edge-case enumerations already in `corner-cases.md`.

A signature line plus a one-sentence behavior note is fine. A 20-line block
showing the implementation is not.

## Process

```
0. THINK — what is this stage trying to deliver, and is the document a
           *contract* the implementer must satisfy or a *draft solution*
           pre-written for them? Record one sentence; do NOT skip.

1. READ  — STAGE_FILE in full (single file, ≤ 500 lines).

2. STRUCTURE CHECK — verify each of the six required sections is present
                     (case-insensitive heading match). Missing required
                     section other than #4 (Public signatures, optional)
                     → MAJOR finding "missing section: <name>".

3. CODE-DENSITY CHECK — find every fenced block (```...```).
                       For each fence:
                         a. Count lines between the fences.
                         b. Classify:
                            - signature-only: ≤ 2 lines AND contains no `{` body
                              opening on the signature line OR balanced empty
                              braces — OK.
                            - full-body: 3+ lines AND contains `{` ... `}` with
                              non-trivial content (not just `// ...`).
                       Fail conditions (each = MAJOR):
                         - any single full-body block ≥ 5 lines
                         - cumulative full-body lines / total file lines > 25 %
                         - more than 1 full-body test fence anywhere in the file

4. DUPLICATION CHECK — scan the stage prose for these smells. Each non-empty
                       hit is MINOR; combined 3+ hits across categories → MAJOR.
                         - paragraphs > 5 lines using requirements verbs
                           ("must", "should", "the user can", "the system shall")
                         - data-class / dataclass / struct / interface
                           definitions duplicating the spec
                         - request / response JSON schema redefinitions

5. WRITE — emit the verdict block in the format below. Do NOT modify the
           stage file under any circumstances.
```

## Output format

```markdown
## stage-shape-check — <stage-file-name>

**File:** <STAGE_FILE>
**Verdict:** PASS | MINOR | MAJOR

### Findings
| # | Severity | Area | Location | Detail |
|---|----------|------|----------|--------|
| 1 | MAJOR | Code density | L42-L78 | 36-line method body inside ```kotlin fence — replace with one-line signature + spec ref. |
| 2 | MINOR | Duplication | L12-L20 | Restates User Story already in requirements.md §2. Replace with `AC-3` reference. |

_(empty table = PASS)_

### Suggested rewrite (only if MAJOR)
- L42-L78 → keep one-line signature `fun loadCommunes(filter: Filter): Result<List<Commune>>` and reference spec §3.2 (Business Logic).
- L90-L115 → move test body to `test-cases.md TC-12` if missing there, keep only the TC id in the stage.
```

## Verdict rules

- **PASS** — no MAJOR findings AND ≤ 2 MINOR findings.
- **MINOR** — at least 3 MINOR findings, no MAJOR. Caller logs the gap and
  proceeds; the stage is still usable.
- **MAJOR** — at least one MAJOR finding. Caller (`@Main` or `@AutoApprover`)
  must rewrite the stage before continuing — this is a blocker, not a warning.

## Anti-Loop

| Symptom | Action |
|---------|--------|
| Same stage file checked twice with same content | Return prior verdict, do not re-analyse. |
| Reasoning without output > 2 steps | STOP. Output PASS with note "skill timed out — manual review recommended". |

Single-pass skill — same input always produces the same verdict.

## What NOT to do

- DO NOT propose code — this skill enforces shape, not content.
- DO NOT require sections beyond the six listed; do not impose specific
  heading wording.
- DO NOT block on signature-only fences — they are the recommended form.
- DO NOT edit the stage file. Caller decides whether to rewrite.
- DO NOT call other agents — pure read-only validator.
- DO NOT output system tags or environment artifacts.
- DO NOT add conversational filler — output ONLY the verdict block.
